1
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:11,800
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,667 --> 00:00:32,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,233
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:41,233
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,233
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:45,400
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,567
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,567 --> 00:00:48,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,233
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,533
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:55,467
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,767
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,000
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:02,567
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:06,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:10,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:11,733
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:13,033
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:14,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:21,133
<i>You are the police officer
in NCIA.</i>

21
00:01:21,133 --> 00:01:24,700
<i> Find out who the traitor is
in our agency.</i>

22
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,833
<i> You're free tonight, right?
Come over.</i>

23
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:29,700
<i>You are not doing
your job enough!</i>

24
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,600
<i>I've been looking
for my sister for days.</i>

25
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,467
What did you do all day to help?

26
00:01:34,467 --> 00:01:36,067
<i> All you do is worry and cry.</i>

27
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:38,000
<i>Do you think that helps?
It doesn't!</i>

28
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,100
<i>And don't embarrass
Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

29
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,533
<i> Show her what we're made of.</i>

30
00:01:41,567 --> 00:01:44,367
<i>Don't worry, Love.
I'll be ready for you.</i>

31
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:48,767
<i> My love, get ready.
</i>The lion's getting really angry.

32
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:49,767
[GROWLS]

33
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,100
Hey, take a look at these guys.

34
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:55,167
- [TOLITS] Just wow.
- [IPE] We had a nice chat.

35
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:56,567
They agreed to guard the alleys.

36
00:01:56,567 --> 00:01:58,367
And now these bastards
are drunk.

37
00:01:58,367 --> 00:01:59,833
Let's wake them up.

38
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:01,133
I'll take care of this.
Stay there.

39
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,700
You sure?

40
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,067
These jerks.

41
00:02:05,067 --> 00:02:07,700
There's a fire! There's a fire!

42
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:08,967
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:08,967 --> 00:02:10,133
- It's not working.
- Not working, man.

44
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:11,733
Step aside. I'll handle this.

45
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:16,700
There's a thief!
There are five of them! Look!

46
00:02:16,733 --> 00:02:17,867
Still not working.

47
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:19,433
- They're in deep slumber.
- Here, let me.

48
00:02:19,433 --> 00:02:23,000
Let me try my trick.
They'll wake up for sure.

49
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,100
Keep the drinks coming!

50
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,367
Where? Where?

51
00:02:28,367 --> 00:02:30,500
- See?
- There we go.

52
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,967
You drunk bastards.

53
00:02:31,967 --> 00:02:34,433
We had a deal.

54
00:02:34,433 --> 00:02:36,300
You said you'd keep an eye
on the alleys.

55
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:39,867
You heard about the shootout
on Soriano Street, right?

56
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:42,333
We asked you to do this

57
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:44,967
so we don't get involved
in those outsider fights.

58
00:02:44,967 --> 00:02:47,067
- And now what?
- [MUSIC TURNS PENSIVE]

59
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,400
I'm sorry.
We'll make it up to you.

60
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,633
Let's go.

61
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:51,467
- Go.
- Go home.

62
00:02:51,467 --> 00:02:53,200
[TOLITS] Hey, you. Leave it.

63
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,867
Watch it.

64
00:02:54,867 --> 00:02:57,267
- Go home.
- Can barely get up.

65
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,200
Go. No detours!

66
00:03:01,133 --> 00:03:03,633
Are we going to tell
Gabo about this?

67
00:03:03,633 --> 00:03:06,967
This might just make him worry.
I don't think we should.

68
00:03:07,533 --> 00:03:09,033
We'll find a replacement.

69
00:03:09,033 --> 00:03:11,967
Binoy, stay here for now.

70
00:03:11,967 --> 00:03:14,433
Bong and I will find men
to guard the alleys.

71
00:03:14,433 --> 00:03:16,667
- Okay. Let's part ways.
- Okay, be careful.

72
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:18,833
- We'll go this way.
- What now?

73
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,500
You're on a diet?

74
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:23,300
How does that sound?

75
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,967
We'll close the deal
at 10,000 pesos.

76
00:03:25,967 --> 00:03:28,433
10,000 pesos. And then,

77
00:03:28,433 --> 00:03:30,867
you can drink beer here
for free.

78
00:03:33,367 --> 00:03:34,433
Beer, please!

79
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:36,800
[CHUCKLES]

80
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,867
Boss.

81
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,100
Here's your beer.

82
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,133
- [PAQUITO] Nice.
- [BETCHAY] Right?

83
00:03:42,133 --> 00:03:44,933
It's still early and the bar's
already packed!

84
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:46,733
Great, right, Manager?

85
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:49,133
- You're good.
- [BETCHAY CHUCKLES]

86
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,833
[DIDAY] Kulas! You animal!

87
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:53,367
- [ESTONG] Ma!
- [BETCHAY] Diday!

88
00:03:53,367 --> 00:03:55,133
- [ESTONG] Ma!
- [BETCHAY] Diday! Hold on!

89
00:03:55,167 --> 00:03:57,100
I'll kill you!

90
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:58,067
Ma!

91
00:03:58,067 --> 00:03:59,900
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

92
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,133
You're going to leave me
for that woman?!

93
00:04:07,633 --> 00:04:09,367
Don't make a scene here!

94
00:04:09,367 --> 00:04:12,800
Diday, calm down! Chill out!

95
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:14,733
I saw Kulas with my two eyes!

96
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:18,033
Where?
Kulas isn't here!

97
00:04:18,033 --> 00:04:20,800
- Don't make a scene here!
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,533
Turn on the lights.

99
00:04:22,533 --> 00:04:24,500
See? Where?

100
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,500
Kulas isn't here. Look!

101
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,833
Did you really see him?
You're unbelievable.

102
00:04:28,867 --> 00:04:30,267
- [DIDAY] Betchay!
- What?

103
00:04:30,267 --> 00:04:33,233
If I found out you're tolerating
his cheating...

104
00:04:33,233 --> 00:04:37,100
I'm not tolerating
anything, Diday.

105
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,233
Oh, Estong, I think you should
bring your mom home.

106
00:04:39,233 --> 00:04:41,267
She might not be seeing well.

107
00:04:41,267 --> 00:04:43,200
- Ma, let's go. He's not here.
- Come on, guys.

108
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,533
Kulas isn't here.
He's not here!

109
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:47,267
- Kulas isn't here.
- Let's go!

110
00:04:47,267 --> 00:04:49,600
Kulas doesn't come here.

111
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:52,933
Kulas! I'll wait for you
at home, you bastard!

112
00:04:52,933 --> 00:04:54,867
[BETCHAY]
Maybe he's somewhere else.

113
00:04:54,867 --> 00:04:58,700
Let's talk outside. Come on.
Let's talk there.

114
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:01,600
Breathe. Calm down.
Let's talk here.

115
00:05:01,633 --> 00:05:02,900
Calm down, Ma. Sit down.

116
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:05,300
Here. Drink some water.

117
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:06,400
Come on.

118
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:09,967
You didn't have to make a scene.
I have customers.

119
00:05:09,967 --> 00:05:12,133
Go home and get some sleep.

120
00:05:12,133 --> 00:05:14,233
If you're having problems
with your husband,

121
00:05:14,233 --> 00:05:16,400
please talk about it at home.

122
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,533
- Come on.
- Let's go home, Ma.

123
00:05:18,533 --> 00:05:21,200
Say hi to my friend Gloria
for me.

124
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:23,700
- Ma! Your mouth!
- Who's Gloria?

125
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:26,433
- Ma! Oh, Ma! Let's go!
- Diday, who's that? Diday!

126
00:05:26,433 --> 00:05:27,733
Gloria who?

127
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:28,933
Psst! Hey!

128
00:05:28,933 --> 00:05:33,133
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:34,200
[MUSIC FADES]

130
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,633
[GABO] Meow!

131
00:05:35,667 --> 00:05:37,300
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:38,733
[GABO] Meow!

133
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:42,000
Who is it?

134
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,033
[GABO GROWLS]

135
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:45,367
I'm a lion!

136
00:05:45,367 --> 00:05:47,700
[GABO GROWLS]

137
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:49,700
- What are you talking about?
- [GABO GROWLS]

138
00:05:51,033 --> 00:05:52,067
You said earlier...

139
00:05:53,533 --> 00:05:55,100
that you want us to make a baby.

140
00:05:56,167 --> 00:05:57,767
I'm ready.

141
00:05:57,767 --> 00:05:59,200
I'm a lion!

142
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:00,833
[SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

143
00:06:00,833 --> 00:06:01,867
Baby...

144
00:06:02,867 --> 00:06:04,133
I told you...

145
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,400
we'd be making a baby, remember?

146
00:06:10,867 --> 00:06:11,933
This is it.

147
00:06:13,633 --> 00:06:15,600
Uh, hold on. Hold on.

148
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,267
It's just that...

149
00:06:19,867 --> 00:06:22,300
I still can't remember anything.

150
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:24,333
I don't even remember you.

151
00:06:24,333 --> 00:06:25,567
Maybe you can...

152
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,600
give me more time.

153
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:31,700
Just until my memory comes back.

154
00:06:32,367 --> 00:06:35,200
Then we'll go back
to how we were.

155
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:39,200
Love. [CHUCKLES DEFEATEDLY]

156
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:41,767
You were excited
to have a child earlier.

157
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:44,867
Then you suddenly
changed your mind.

158
00:06:44,867 --> 00:06:47,167
Maybe we can still,

159
00:06:47,167 --> 00:06:48,700
you know...

160
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,700
[SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

161
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:52,967
Uh...

162
00:06:54,167 --> 00:06:56,633
we'll get to that soon.

163
00:06:56,633 --> 00:06:58,933
I really thought

164
00:06:58,933 --> 00:07:02,400
the lion and the tiger
would get on it.

165
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:04,733
[GABO GROWLING]

166
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:07,000
Oh! [SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

167
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,233
[GABO GROWLS]

168
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,867
You can still change your mind.

169
00:07:11,867 --> 00:07:14,033
- [SAM STAMMERS]
- The lion is so ready.

170
00:07:14,033 --> 00:07:17,000
Sorry, really.

171
00:07:17,033 --> 00:07:20,267
N-Next time, okay?

172
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:24,100
Fine. If...

173
00:07:25,033 --> 00:07:26,400
If you're not ready,
that's okay.

174
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,700
You know how much I love

175
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:31,233
and respect you.

176
00:07:32,367 --> 00:07:34,067
That's not what I'm after.

177
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:38,100
What matters to me
is your happiness.

178
00:07:41,133 --> 00:07:42,733
But, Love,

179
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:44,867
please think about it.

180
00:07:44,867 --> 00:07:48,300
Maybe you're just confused
right now.

181
00:07:48,333 --> 00:07:49,367
Or baffled.

182
00:07:50,233 --> 00:07:52,967
Maybe once we're lying
beside each other,

183
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,133
you'd realize, you know...

184
00:07:57,233 --> 00:07:58,533
- ...you've forgotten about it.
- Ah...

185
00:07:58,533 --> 00:08:02,400
Or suddenly
you feel uncomfortable.

186
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,800
Just tap me.

187
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,767
Okay, let's go to sleep,
shall we?

188
00:08:06,567 --> 00:08:07,667
Good night.

189
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:18,767
Love you.

190
00:08:19,667 --> 00:08:21,100
Hmm.

191
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:22,267
Love you.

192
00:08:23,733 --> 00:08:27,400
[GABO]
I really thought it'd happen.

193
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:33,933
I even brushed my teeth
and scrubbed my body.

194
00:08:33,933 --> 00:08:37,200
[SAM] Oh, thank God.

195
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:40,367
<i> I thought he was going to
take advantage of me.</i>

196
00:08:40,367 --> 00:08:44,900
<i>Lord, please protect me
while I'm staying here.</i>

197
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:47,000
<i> Especially from this guy.</i>

198
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,833
<i>I hope he doesn't
try to touch me.</i>

199
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:55,667
<i>If he does, I have no choice
but to fight back</i>

200
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:58,067
<i> and blow my cover.</i>

201
00:08:59,867 --> 00:09:02,567
[GABO]<i> I would never
</i> take advantage of you.

202
00:09:02,567 --> 00:09:04,233
<i> I was just kidding.</i>

203
00:09:04,867 --> 00:09:08,533
<i>Don't worry, Gloria,
I respect you.</i>

204
00:09:08,533 --> 00:09:10,367
<i> And I promise you,</i>

205
00:09:10,367 --> 00:09:12,467
<i>that while
you're under our roof,</i>

206
00:09:12,467 --> 00:09:16,267
<i> I will love and respect you.</i>

207
00:09:16,267 --> 00:09:19,767
<i> I hope that one day,
when the truth comes out,</i>

208
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:22,000
<i>you will still accept me
and forgive me</i>

209
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,400
<i>for all the lies I told you
to protect you.</i>

210
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:32,367
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

211
00:09:38,067 --> 00:09:39,700
- [CUSTOMER] Let's go home!
- Betchay!

212
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:41,700
- Yes, boss?
- You continue to impress me.

213
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:45,067
- You managed to fool Diday.
- Of course! [CHUCKLES]

214
00:09:45,067 --> 00:09:48,300
Paquito made the right choice
in making you manager!

215
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:49,667
You got that right!

216
00:09:49,667 --> 00:09:51,400
- Kulas.
- Thanks, Betchay.

217
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,700
Who is this Gloria
Diday mentioned?

218
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:55,167
Who is Gloria?

219
00:09:55,167 --> 00:09:57,467
I have no idea, Betchay.

220
00:09:57,467 --> 00:09:58,567
I'll head home now.

221
00:09:58,567 --> 00:10:00,467
Wait, you haven't paid yet.

222
00:10:00,467 --> 00:10:03,533
- How much is his bill?
- 800 pesos.

223
00:10:03,567 --> 00:10:06,767
Make sure you don't slip up
and say you were here.

224
00:10:06,767 --> 00:10:08,700
If you're going to cheat on
your wife,

225
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:11,200
don't let her catch you!

226
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,133
- I'm not cheating on my wife.
- Really?

227
00:10:13,133 --> 00:10:15,133
- What are you doing here then?
- [PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

228
00:10:15,133 --> 00:10:18,833
The man's just trying
something new, Betchay!

229
00:10:18,833 --> 00:10:21,333
You'd get sick of eating
the same dish every day,

230
00:10:21,333 --> 00:10:23,267
wouldn't you?

231
00:10:23,267 --> 00:10:24,567
[CHUCKLES]

232
00:10:25,533 --> 00:10:28,200
Betchay, are you
getting sick of Rudy?

233
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:30,433
Why are you asking me?

234
00:10:30,433 --> 00:10:32,333
We were talking about Kulas
over here.

235
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:34,933
Have you grown tired
of Diday, Kulas?

236
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:36,733
No way!
I love her!

237
00:10:36,733 --> 00:10:38,567
Even though she wanted
to chop off your head?

238
00:10:38,567 --> 00:10:39,900
That's right.

239
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:42,200
Now that's love.

240
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:44,067
No matter how angry
they make you,

241
00:10:44,067 --> 00:10:47,367
you still love them
and choose them in the end.

242
00:10:47,367 --> 00:10:49,800
- I'll go ahead now.
- Oh, all right.

243
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,933
Move along.

244
00:10:50,933 --> 00:10:52,067
[PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

245
00:10:52,067 --> 00:10:57,400
You know, Betchay,
I would choose you.

246
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,667
Cool watch, boss!

247
00:10:59,667 --> 00:11:02,233
- You can have it.
- Oh, it isn't for me.

248
00:11:02,233 --> 00:11:04,167
I want to give it to Rudy.
How much is it?

249
00:11:04,167 --> 00:11:07,200
- It's expensive.
- He's worth it.

250
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,400
And I want to give him
a special gift.

251
00:11:09,433 --> 00:11:10,967
It's his birthday tomorrow.

252
00:11:10,967 --> 00:11:13,167
Betchay, get back to work.

253
00:11:15,533 --> 00:11:18,133
- Hey, are we having fun?
- Of course.

254
00:11:19,267 --> 00:11:23,100
- Oh, Boss Paquito.
- Yeah?

255
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:25,933
Betchay, are you
heading home already?

256
00:11:25,933 --> 00:11:27,700
Uh...

257
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:30,267
Are you clocking out early,
Manager?

258
00:11:30,267 --> 00:11:31,300
Of course not.

259
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:34,900
No. I'll be working all night.

260
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:39,500
But I was wondering if I could
take tomorrow off.

261
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:40,767
It's Rudy's birthday.

262
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,833
You know, family comes first.

263
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:44,900
You just got promoted,

264
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:46,200
and you already
want to take time off?

265
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,567
Alright, how about this?

266
00:11:47,567 --> 00:11:49,933
Um, I'll just come in
a bit later.

267
00:11:49,933 --> 00:11:53,100
I'll report straight to work
after Rudy's party.

268
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,667
Please.

269
00:11:54,667 --> 00:11:56,800
Please, boss.

270
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:59,333
Why are you making time for him?

271
00:11:59,333 --> 00:12:01,400
I thought you were mad at him?

272
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:05,467
Well... he's warming up to me.

273
00:12:05,467 --> 00:12:07,400
I guess he's starting
to regret what he did.

274
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:10,833
I bet it's because he's
hiding something from you.

275
00:12:10,833 --> 00:12:13,733
What? That's absurd!

276
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,200
No, it isn't.

277
00:12:15,233 --> 00:12:16,967
Please, Paquito.

278
00:12:16,967 --> 00:12:19,233
Just this once.

279
00:12:19,233 --> 00:12:22,100
Pretty please?

280
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:23,200
- Hmm?
- Ugh.

281
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,067
- Fine.
- [BETCHAY GUSHES, CLAPS]

282
00:12:25,067 --> 00:12:27,700
Alright. Back to work.

283
00:12:28,367 --> 00:12:30,600
Thank you.

284
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:35,833
You can have any woman
you want.

285
00:12:35,833 --> 00:12:38,200
Why are you still
fawning over Betchay?

286
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,867
Well...

287
00:12:39,867 --> 00:12:45,633
I was humiliated when
Betchay chose Rudy over me.

288
00:12:45,633 --> 00:12:47,933
So I need to settle the score.

289
00:12:50,233 --> 00:12:52,133
And you think
you'll win Betchay over?

290
00:12:52,133 --> 00:12:55,500
[SCOFFS] Romy, I'll get her.

291
00:12:55,500 --> 00:13:01,333
Remember,
I can get whatever I want.

292
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:03,333
It remains to be seen.

293
00:13:05,433 --> 00:13:07,600
Ma'am, Ms. Catacutan is here.

294
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,600
Why did you summon me?

295
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,533
What do you want?

296
00:13:14,033 --> 00:13:16,467
- [SLAPS]
- [PIA GASPS, GRUNTS]

297
00:13:16,467 --> 00:13:17,533
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [DEBORAH GRUNTS]

298
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:21,100
[PIA EXCLAIMS, GRUNTS]

299
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYS]

300
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:27,000
We already gave you
75 million pesos.

301
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,067
But you didn't keep
your end of the deal!

302
00:13:30,067 --> 00:13:34,400
My son was still transferred
to a maximum-security facility!

303
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:37,933
I had no control
over his transfer!

304
00:13:37,933 --> 00:13:40,167
Since you're useless,

305
00:13:40,167 --> 00:13:43,333
you'll make up for it
with your life!

306
00:13:43,333 --> 00:13:45,500
Wait a minute.
Wait a minute.

307
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,500
I can still fix this.

308
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:49,833
I can still fix this.
Let me fix this.

309
00:13:49,833 --> 00:13:51,533
I'll make things right!

310
00:13:51,533 --> 00:13:53,333
Does the NCIA know that

311
00:13:53,333 --> 00:13:56,433
our group tried to
break Victor out?

312
00:13:56,467 --> 00:14:00,433
You are their only suspect.

313
00:14:00,433 --> 00:14:04,933
But what matters is there's
no evidence tied back to you.

314
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:13,433
Do you think Sir Seb is right?

315
00:14:14,367 --> 00:14:17,733
That Ma'am Sam's in hiding
so she can move on her own?

316
00:14:17,733 --> 00:14:21,167
That would mean
she's alive and safe.

317
00:14:21,167 --> 00:14:23,167
But she could at least tell us.

318
00:14:23,167 --> 00:14:24,867
Look at the bright side.

319
00:14:24,867 --> 00:14:28,167
Victor Zafra is now in
a maximum-security facility.

320
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,300
But there are no leads
on Ma'am Sam's whereabouts.

321
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:32,433
The investigation
is still ongoing.

322
00:14:32,433 --> 00:14:34,033
Don't you think
something strange is going on?

323
00:14:34,033 --> 00:14:36,133
First, Mr. Chan was killed
in an ambush.

324
00:14:36,133 --> 00:14:38,567
Then, Victor's convoy
was also ambushed

325
00:14:38,567 --> 00:14:40,667
in an attempt to break him out.

326
00:14:40,667 --> 00:14:42,900
Karen, you seem to be
jumping the gun here.

327
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:44,533
What are you trying to imply?

328
00:14:44,533 --> 00:14:46,833
It's like Mr. Chan's killer

329
00:14:46,833 --> 00:14:48,700
and whoever attempted
to help Victor escape

330
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:50,733
know how we operate here.

331
00:14:50,733 --> 00:14:56,367
The Zafras are capable of
obtaining intel from the inside.

332
00:14:56,367 --> 00:14:58,367
So we have to be careful.

333
00:14:58,367 --> 00:15:03,100
We have to keep confidential
information among ourselves.

334
00:15:03,133 --> 00:15:05,633
Karen, you're being paranoid.

335
00:15:05,633 --> 00:15:08,567
I'd rather be paranoid
than lose more colleagues.

336
00:15:08,567 --> 00:15:14,400
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

337
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:16,567
- Who is this?
- I can do it.

338
00:15:16,567 --> 00:15:18,700
Our mole at the NCIA.

339
00:15:19,567 --> 00:15:21,467
You're from the NCIA?!

340
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:26,467
Why didn't you help
my brother escape?!

341
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:28,767
Lucas! Enough!

342
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:33,800
She knows she messed up.

343
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:36,167
Don't you, Pia?

344
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,600
[WEAKLY] Yes.

345
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,133
Weapons down.

346
00:15:39,133 --> 00:15:40,767
Let me go! [GRUNTS]

347
00:15:43,267 --> 00:15:46,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

348
00:15:46,533 --> 00:15:50,900
Why didn't you tell us that
NLEA would be escorting

349
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,733
Victor's convoy?

350
00:15:53,733 --> 00:15:58,700
NLEA was there
on General Jacinto's orders.

351
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:00,467
I knew it.

352
00:16:00,467 --> 00:16:04,033
And General Jacinto
was the one who oversaw

353
00:16:04,033 --> 00:16:07,467
Victor's transfer
to maximum security.

354
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:11,267
Ricardo is getting revenge for
what happened to his daughter.

355
00:16:12,467 --> 00:16:15,367
Our son in exchange
for his daughter.

356
00:16:15,367 --> 00:16:17,200
Don't worry, Pa.

357
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:19,167
Victor's just in jail.

358
00:16:19,167 --> 00:16:21,200
But Samantha's dead.

359
00:16:22,367 --> 00:16:26,233
What's the latest development
on Samantha Jacinto's case?

360
00:16:26,233 --> 00:16:29,067
They're still looking for her.

361
00:16:29,067 --> 00:16:32,567
Those morons think
Jacinto is still alive.

362
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:33,633
[LUCAS SCOFFS]

363
00:16:33,633 --> 00:16:35,133
Impossible!

364
00:16:35,133 --> 00:16:38,100
The only thing they'll find
is her rotting corpse.

365
00:16:39,433 --> 00:16:43,333
You'll keep us updated...

366
00:16:44,667 --> 00:16:45,667
right?

367
00:16:48,067 --> 00:16:50,033
[TENSE MUSIC SWELLS]

368
00:16:50,033 --> 00:16:53,700
We'll keep our word
if you keep yours.

369
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:56,567
But the moment you cross us,

370
00:16:57,733 --> 00:17:00,567
you won't have time
to regret it.

371
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,500
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

372
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,967
Go!

373
00:17:07,967 --> 00:17:13,667
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

374
00:17:13,667 --> 00:17:14,833
[PIA HUFFS]

375
00:17:16,933 --> 00:17:19,200
[GRUNTS ANGRILY]

376
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:21,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

377
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:27,067
Ricardo couldn't do anything
when he went here.

378
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:30,600
So he used his position
and influence to retaliate.

379
00:17:33,467 --> 00:17:34,400
[GLASS THUDS]

380
00:17:35,033 --> 00:17:39,033
Any parent would bare
their fangs

381
00:17:39,033 --> 00:17:41,833
when it comes to their children.

382
00:17:41,833 --> 00:17:43,133
But even back then...

383
00:17:44,333 --> 00:17:46,433
Ricardo's always been
a bastard.

384
00:17:46,433 --> 00:17:47,667
He's sly!

385
00:17:47,667 --> 00:17:51,633
He plays well enough
to deceive a lot of people.

386
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:53,700
But I know him.

387
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:57,667
I know every single one
of his secrets.

388
00:17:57,667 --> 00:18:00,133
Someday, I'll use
all that information...

389
00:18:00,967 --> 00:18:02,533
to destroy him.

390
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:07,933
If he knows how to play,
so should we.

391
00:18:07,933 --> 00:18:12,700
But let's not give the enemy
the fight that he wants.

392
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:16,033
- What do you mean?
- We stop fighting.

393
00:18:17,967 --> 00:18:19,000
For now.

394
00:18:19,667 --> 00:18:24,833
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

395
00:18:24,867 --> 00:18:27,833
Let's take care
of our business first.

396
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:32,833
We've lost too much
since Victor was imprisoned.

397
00:18:35,233 --> 00:18:37,267
We need to recover.

398
00:18:37,267 --> 00:18:41,733
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:18:41,733 --> 00:18:42,667
[GLASSES CLINK]

400
00:18:47,433 --> 00:18:54,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

401
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:00,633
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

402
00:19:02,467 --> 00:19:03,400
[DOOR SHUTS]

403
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:15,267
[PAPERS RUSTLING]

404
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:20,867
[PAPERS RUSTLING]

405
00:19:22,067 --> 00:19:23,100
[LAMP SWITCH CLICKS]

406
00:19:23,733 --> 00:19:29,700
[FOLDERS RUSTLING]

407
00:19:33,967 --> 00:19:34,967
[DRAWER SLIDES OPEN]

408
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,467
[FOLDER THUDS]

409
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,667
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

410
00:19:50,933 --> 00:19:57,900
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]
- [PAPER RUSTLING]

411
00:19:59,233 --> 00:20:00,267
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

412
00:20:00,267 --> 00:20:01,700
[PAPERS RUSTLE]

413
00:20:02,733 --> 00:20:09,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

414
00:20:16,467 --> 00:20:17,767
[LAMP SWITCH CLICKS]

415
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:27,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

416
00:20:33,833 --> 00:20:34,967
[DOOR CREAKS SHUT]

417
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:38,600
Limbaga?

418
00:20:40,567 --> 00:20:42,067
Why are you here?

419
00:20:42,067 --> 00:20:43,733
I just went back for something.

420
00:20:44,367 --> 00:20:46,067
What about you?
Why are you here?

421
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:47,533
Um...

422
00:20:48,167 --> 00:20:50,000
Mr. Delgado rushed me
to do something.

423
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,467
I just placed it on his desk.

424
00:20:52,133 --> 00:20:53,400
Ah...

425
00:20:55,467 --> 00:20:56,900
What happened to your lips?

426
00:20:58,100 --> 00:20:59,033
Uh...

427
00:21:00,233 --> 00:21:01,567
I hit myself with my tumbler.

428
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:04,233
Mind your own business.

429
00:21:04,833 --> 00:21:09,500
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

430
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,733
- Oh!
- Betchay!

431
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:18,933
Why are you still here?
It's already morning!

432
00:21:18,933 --> 00:21:22,667
You're going to buy a gift
for Rudy, right?

433
00:21:22,667 --> 00:21:25,167
- Yes.
- I can come with you!

434
00:21:25,167 --> 00:21:28,133
Oh, I don't want to bother you.
I can do this myself!

435
00:21:28,133 --> 00:21:33,667
Betchay, I know what gifts
men want.

436
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:36,633
[BETCHAY CHUCKLING]

437
00:21:36,633 --> 00:21:40,067
It's fine.
I know what Rudy wants.

438
00:21:40,067 --> 00:21:41,900
And you don't have to do me
any more favors.

439
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:46,067
Allowing me to arrive late
later tonight is enough.

440
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:47,600
Thank you, sir!

441
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:52,567
Come on.

442
00:21:54,033 --> 00:21:59,667
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

443
00:21:59,667 --> 00:22:01,067
[PILLOWS THUMP]

444
00:22:17,067 --> 00:22:18,067
[MAX SIGHS]

445
00:22:18,067 --> 00:22:24,533
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

446
00:22:24,533 --> 00:22:25,800
Mom?

447
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:27,267
Why did you sleep here?

448
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:29,833
I miss my daughter.

449
00:22:31,533 --> 00:22:32,967
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

450
00:22:34,767 --> 00:22:38,933
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

451
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:42,500
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

452
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:48,267
Mom, with everything
that's happening right now,

453
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:53,800
we're all feeling
very emotional.

454
00:22:54,267 --> 00:22:56,833
That's why sometimes
we can't control

455
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,800
the things we say.

456
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,167
We don't mean to sometimes,

457
00:23:03,167 --> 00:23:06,033
but we end up saying
things that hurt.

458
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:09,233
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

459
00:23:10,833 --> 00:23:12,033
Mom...

460
00:23:13,867 --> 00:23:16,967
You know why
I'm saying this, right?

461
00:23:17,567 --> 00:23:18,767
[MAX SNIFFLING]

462
00:23:18,767 --> 00:23:20,733
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

463
00:23:22,533 --> 00:23:27,500
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

464
00:23:28,467 --> 00:23:30,300
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

465
00:23:33,967 --> 00:23:35,467
What are we going to tell Gabo?

466
00:23:35,467 --> 00:23:37,100
Don't worry, we've got
plenty to cook.

467
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:38,700
Hey, Gloria.

468
00:23:38,700 --> 00:23:40,600
- What are you doing, dear?
- [DANTE] Hija.

469
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:42,900
Don't do that.
It's embarrassing.

470
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:44,133
She's cleaning.

471
00:23:44,133 --> 00:23:46,733
It's okay. I'm the one
who's embarrassed.

472
00:23:46,733 --> 00:23:48,367
I'm not a guest here, anyway.

473
00:23:48,367 --> 00:23:50,600
And besides,
I'm sorry about this, okay?

474
00:23:50,600 --> 00:23:52,033
I changed the curtains.

475
00:23:52,033 --> 00:23:54,633
I noticed you had
some extra ones.

476
00:23:54,633 --> 00:23:55,900
Oh, yeah, you're right.

477
00:23:55,933 --> 00:23:58,567
Oh, dear, we were
supposed to do that.

478
00:23:58,567 --> 00:24:00,167
You should get some rest.

479
00:24:00,167 --> 00:24:02,533
Your wound hasn't healed yet.

480
00:24:02,533 --> 00:24:03,967
Exactly. Give me that rag.

481
00:24:03,967 --> 00:24:05,467
I'll finish what you're doing.

482
00:24:05,467 --> 00:24:07,267
Yes, go on.
We'll take care of it.

483
00:24:07,267 --> 00:24:10,367
Okay. I'll just finish
what I'm doing in the kitchen.

484
00:24:10,367 --> 00:24:11,533
[DANTE] Okay, go ahead.

485
00:24:12,567 --> 00:24:14,900
This girl, honestly.

486
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:16,133
Good morning, sir.

487
00:24:23,767 --> 00:24:24,867
[MAX] Dad.

488
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:26,700
Hi.

489
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:29,500
Why aren't you eating?

490
00:24:29,533 --> 00:24:31,200
I don't feel like it.

491
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,000
You still have to eat.

492
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:36,500
Don't neglect yourself.

493
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:37,633
You and Mom.

494
00:24:38,433 --> 00:24:40,900
Twinkle, please take
some food up to Mom.

495
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:42,367
- Yes, ma'am.
- Thank you.

496
00:24:42,367 --> 00:24:43,633
[SIGHS]

497
00:24:43,633 --> 00:24:47,400
Max, I know Sam's
alive and safe.

498
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,500
That's what I believe too, Dad.

499
00:24:49,500 --> 00:24:51,600
But why hasn't she
contacted us?

500
00:24:51,600 --> 00:24:54,133
Is it because she's still
holding a grudge against me,

501
00:24:54,133 --> 00:24:58,000
or because she's enjoying
her newfound freedom?

502
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,733
I don't think it's like that.

503
00:24:59,733 --> 00:25:02,433
Dad, this isn't going
to help our case.

504
00:25:02,467 --> 00:25:04,633
And especially
not your well-being.

505
00:25:05,267 --> 00:25:07,633
What if, before we even
bring Sam home,

506
00:25:07,633 --> 00:25:10,267
you end up getting sick
and hospitalized?

507
00:25:11,567 --> 00:25:13,367
You know, I admit that...

508
00:25:14,833 --> 00:25:16,400
I've made a lot
of mistakes, too.

509
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:18,667
But when I did those things,
at the time,

510
00:25:18,667 --> 00:25:21,433
I knew they were
the right thing to do.

511
00:25:21,433 --> 00:25:23,567
Nobody wanted this to happen,

512
00:25:23,567 --> 00:25:25,367
and none of this
has anything to do

513
00:25:25,367 --> 00:25:27,467
with how you raised
Sam and me.

514
00:25:27,467 --> 00:25:31,500
So please, don't blame yourself.

515
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,500
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

516
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:36,133
[DANTE GRUNTING]

517
00:25:36,967 --> 00:25:39,600
Oh, sorry. I'm just
fixing these curtains.

518
00:25:41,033 --> 00:25:43,533
Why is the house so tidy?

519
00:25:43,533 --> 00:25:45,467
Are we expecting someone?

520
00:25:45,467 --> 00:25:47,100
I didn't invite anyone over.

521
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:49,667
[MAMENG] When we got here,

522
00:25:49,667 --> 00:25:52,267
we found her fixing up
the house.

523
00:25:52,767 --> 00:25:53,900
Why?

524
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:57,433
- [GLASSES CLINK]
- [MAMENG] Well...

525
00:25:57,433 --> 00:25:59,167
Oh. Good morning.

526
00:25:59,833 --> 00:26:01,133
Good morning.

527
00:26:01,133 --> 00:26:02,433
[MAMENG GIGGLES SOFTLY]

528
00:26:03,633 --> 00:26:07,500
I told her to get some rest.

529
00:26:07,500 --> 00:26:08,800
She shouldn't be moving around

530
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:10,967
because her wound
hasn't healed yet.

531
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,733
I'm fine, really.

532
00:26:15,100 --> 00:26:16,700
Uh, Pa?

533
00:26:17,767 --> 00:26:19,667
Happy birthday, by the way.

534
00:26:19,667 --> 00:26:22,100
Oh, that's right!
It's your birthday, brother!

535
00:26:22,100 --> 00:26:23,367
- Oh!
- That's right!

536
00:26:23,367 --> 00:26:25,100
- It's my birthday!
- Your birthday!

537
00:26:25,100 --> 00:26:26,733
- I almost forgot.
- Happy birthday!

538
00:26:26,733 --> 00:26:28,633
Thank you. Thank you.

539
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,700
Wait.

540
00:26:31,700 --> 00:26:33,400
Did you fix up
the living room, too?

541
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,700
Yes.

542
00:26:34,700 --> 00:26:37,233
Don't you like it? I can put
everything back the way it was.

543
00:26:37,233 --> 00:26:38,267
Oh, no, no.

544
00:26:38,267 --> 00:26:39,833
It's beautiful.
I really like it.

545
00:26:39,833 --> 00:26:41,533
- Yeah.
- It feels more spacious.

546
00:26:41,533 --> 00:26:44,533
Yeah, and it's brighter, too.

547
00:26:44,567 --> 00:26:48,700
I should've arranged it
like this a long time ago.

548
00:26:48,700 --> 00:26:49,867
[SAM GIGGLES]

549
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:54,467
I haven't prepared
breakfast yet.

550
00:26:54,833 --> 00:26:55,900
I'm sorry.

551
00:26:55,900 --> 00:26:58,033
Oh, dear,
don't worry about that.

552
00:26:58,033 --> 00:26:59,200
I'll cook.

553
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:01,300
I'll just buy the ingredients.

554
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:03,833
Let me do it, so you can
fix some things around here.

555
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:09,333
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

556
00:27:11,067 --> 00:27:12,167
Oh.

557
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,600
[WHISPERS]
I don't have any money.

558
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:16,267
- Do you have any?
- No.

559
00:27:16,300 --> 00:27:17,467
Uh, dear.

560
00:27:17,467 --> 00:27:19,800
Just put it on the list.
We'll take care of it.

561
00:27:20,667 --> 00:27:22,533
- Okay, I'll take care of it.
- Alright.

562
00:27:22,533 --> 00:27:23,800
Take care.

563
00:27:26,300 --> 00:27:27,833
Did she call you Papa?

564
00:27:27,833 --> 00:27:29,600
- She did!
- You heard her?

565
00:27:30,467 --> 00:27:33,200
- It feels so good.
- Yeah.

566
00:27:33,667 --> 00:27:35,567
- What a nice kid.
- Yeah.

567
00:27:35,567 --> 00:27:36,533
She's both pretty and kind.

568
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:40,800
- [DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE]
- [ROOSTER CROWING]

569
00:27:41,700 --> 00:27:46,300
[BARKING CONTINUES]

570
00:27:46,300 --> 00:27:53,267
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

571
00:27:53,767 --> 00:27:54,833
Gloria?

572
00:27:57,267 --> 00:27:58,533
Gloria?!

573
00:27:58,533 --> 00:27:59,467
Gloria!

574
00:27:59,467 --> 00:28:01,233
Auntie, where's Gloria?

575
00:28:02,367 --> 00:28:04,833
[MAMENG] She went out to buy
some breakfast ingredients.

576
00:28:04,833 --> 00:28:05,967
Why did you let her?

577
00:28:05,967 --> 00:28:07,267
Son, she insisted.

578
00:28:07,267 --> 00:28:08,733
There was no stopping her.

579
00:28:08,733 --> 00:28:13,133
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

580
00:28:13,133 --> 00:28:15,133
[DANTE] Gabo, listen.

581
00:28:15,133 --> 00:28:17,733
When we got back home
from the market,

582
00:28:17,733 --> 00:28:18,933
the whole place
was sparkling clean

583
00:28:18,933 --> 00:28:22,633
and the curtains
had been replaced.

584
00:28:22,667 --> 00:28:24,567
She even said she plans
to cook for us.

585
00:28:24,967 --> 00:28:26,300
[MAMENG] That's true.

586
00:28:26,300 --> 00:28:29,800
Hang on,
what's gotten into Gloria?

587
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:32,867
She's suddenly so restless.

588
00:28:32,867 --> 00:28:34,867
Did something happen last night?

589
00:28:34,867 --> 00:28:36,133
Nothing at all, Auntie.

590
00:28:36,500 --> 00:28:38,300
But we did have a talk.

591
00:28:38,300 --> 00:28:40,200
She shared that she was feeling
awkward around us,

592
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:42,100
because she still doesn't
remember anything.

593
00:28:42,633 --> 00:28:44,867
So today,
she wants to make up for it.

594
00:28:45,533 --> 00:28:48,233
That's probably why she cleaned
and wants to cook for us.

595
00:28:48,233 --> 00:28:50,100
What worries me, Gabo...

596
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:53,100
is that she's clearly
not used to household chores.

597
00:28:53,100 --> 00:28:55,067
She might be struggling.

598
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:58,000
When are you going
to tell her the truth?

599
00:28:58,033 --> 00:29:00,867
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

600
00:29:00,867 --> 00:29:01,833
[GABO STAMMERS]

601
00:29:01,833 --> 00:29:02,933
Auntie...

602
00:29:03,333 --> 00:29:06,700
W-We all know Gloria's life
is still in danger.

603
00:29:07,033 --> 00:29:08,800
There are still men...

604
00:29:09,367 --> 00:29:12,033
roaming around here,
looking for her.

605
00:29:12,033 --> 00:29:14,300
Until I'm certain she's safe,

606
00:29:14,633 --> 00:29:16,733
she'll have to stay
in our house.

607
00:29:17,133 --> 00:29:19,100
Son, I just feel sorry for her.

608
00:29:19,467 --> 00:29:22,533
Maybe she overheard
how Betchay put us down.

609
00:29:22,533 --> 00:29:25,467
And if they see each other
for the first time,

610
00:29:25,467 --> 00:29:27,167
she might become
her next target.

611
00:29:27,167 --> 00:29:29,467
Pa, I won't let that happen.

612
00:29:29,500 --> 00:29:31,733
If Auntie Betchay did that
to Gloria,

613
00:29:32,067 --> 00:29:33,567
we'd have a real problem.

614
00:29:34,300 --> 00:29:38,433
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

615
00:29:38,433 --> 00:29:39,600
[SCREEN DOOR SQUEAKS]

616
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:40,833
[MALE VENDOR] Some onions?

617
00:29:40,833 --> 00:29:41,933
Three of them, please.

618
00:29:41,933 --> 00:29:44,633
- I'll take these, too.
- Sure, here you go.

619
00:29:47,133 --> 00:29:54,133
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" BY
JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

620
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:11,433
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

621
00:30:11,433 --> 00:30:12,900
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

622
00:30:22,133 --> 00:30:23,100
Hey.

623
00:30:23,533 --> 00:30:25,300
Why-- Why did you
wake up so early?

624
00:30:26,500 --> 00:30:27,633
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

625
00:30:27,633 --> 00:30:29,200
I-I could've...

626
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:32,500
picked these up
so you wouldn't have to.

627
00:30:32,933 --> 00:30:34,233
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] It's fine.

628
00:30:34,233 --> 00:30:37,167
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

629
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:38,367
[EXHALES] Let me.

630
00:30:40,267 --> 00:30:47,267
[GENTLE CHIMING SFX]

631
00:30:55,700 --> 00:30:58,067
I'm starting to get frustrated!

632
00:30:58,067 --> 00:31:00,100
<i> I don't know what else to do!</i>

633
00:31:00,100 --> 00:31:03,533
<i>Let me introduce you to the
great Madam Matilda Roselle.</i>

634
00:31:03,533 --> 00:31:06,633
<i> What happened to my daughter?
I want to know!</i>

635
00:31:06,633 --> 00:31:09,800
<i>Sam suffered a
gruesome fate, Isobel!</i>

636
00:31:09,833 --> 00:31:11,633
<i> Sam is gone!</i>

637
00:31:11,633 --> 00:31:14,200
Sam! My daughter can't be dead!

638
00:31:14,200 --> 00:31:17,433
<i>Our neighbors are
doing way too much.</i>

639
00:31:17,433 --> 00:31:18,567
<i> Is that meant for me?</i>

640
00:31:18,567 --> 00:31:20,267
<i> Hey, hey! Hooray!</i>

641
00:31:20,267 --> 00:31:21,400
<i> It's Rudy's birthday.</i>

642
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:22,867
<i> We'll pay them a visit.</i>

643
00:31:22,867 --> 00:31:24,000
[CONFETTI POPS]

644
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:29,367
<i> Who are these guys you claim
can match my level?</i>

645
00:31:29,367 --> 00:31:33,300
Do they measure up to my looks?

646
00:31:33,300 --> 00:31:37,700
<i>Are they as rich
and smart as me?</i>

647
00:31:37,700 --> 00:31:44,700
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

648
00:31:49,067 --> 00:31:50,100
<i> Gabo!</i>

649
00:31:50,100 --> 00:31:51,600
Django and his crew are coming!

650
00:31:52,800 --> 00:31:53,900
<i> Django!</i>

651
00:31:53,900 --> 00:31:55,567
<i>What are you doing here
in Paradise?</i>

652
00:31:57,033 --> 00:32:01,267
<i> We're here to join the fun
at Rudy's birthday!</i>

653
00:32:01,267 --> 00:32:02,933
<i> Who's the lady with you?
She's pretty.</i>
